xarif build: pace MusicBrainz, the Cover Art Archive and BrainzMash below
upstream's rates.

Why: MusicBrainz allows about 1 request per second per IP and declines every
request over it (doc/MusicBrainz_API/Rate_Limiting); an IP that "impacts the
server" may be blocked. This server was cut off on 2026-10-24 after an
experiment ran two MusicBrainz clients from the same address. Upstream's own
rate table records that a coverartarchive.org burst made every MetaBrainz
host refuse the client, and both names resolve to one front door
(142.132.241.153). So: musicbrainz 1.0 -> 0.5/s (operator decision
2026-10-24), coverartarchive 10 -> 1/s. BrainzMash publishes no limit;
upstream forces 10/s, held at 4/s here (operator decision 2026-10-24).

Cost: the first identification of a large library takes about twice as long
on MusicBrainz and 2.5x as long on BrainzMash, and cold cover grids fill
more slowly.

Remove when: never automatically; revisit only with MetaBrainz's agreement.
Tests: cargo test -p droppedneedle-providers --lib shows the same single
failure with and without this patch (cache::tests::
a_fetch_that_met_a_failure_stores_nothing, pre-existing at f65ebf0).

